# `STATECHART-GENRE-SCOPE`: the `statechart` genre header itself. The v0 shape is the header
# token and NOTHING ELSE — the scene vocabulary with its scene meanings, the
# scene default flow (`right`, NOT flowchart's `down`), and no keyword of its
# own. What the genre adds is the READING RULE, which lives in the model as
# `header.genre` and nowhere else: a node here is a state, an edge a
# transition, and no geometry says so.
figdown 0.2 statechart
state locked "LOCKED"
state unlocked "UNLOCKED"
transition locked -[coin]-> unlocked
transition unlocked -[push]-> locked
transition locked -[push]-> locked
